    {
      "id": "0gMNmR8FOvg78gH-93wlF",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 482.71429443359375,
      "y": 217.00003051757812,
      "width": 649,
      "height": 50,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bea",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 946226337,
      "version": 128,
      "versionNonce": 751386721,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1766797812169,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Before starting with spring security we need to understand \nthe importance of security ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Before starting with spring security we need to understand \nthe importance of security ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "61tDpMjOVB5o2ovCpio0X",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 486.71429443359375,
      "y": 331.00006103515625,
      "width": 253,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "beb",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1042945103,
      "version": 25,
      "versionNonce": 825742703,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1766797823135,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Importance of security ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Importance of security ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "ET5Xn3dUOIsVN8NstDD_z",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 485.7877197265625,
      "y": 332.42852783203125,
      "width": 714.99609375,
      "height": 300,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bec",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2110861505,
      "version": 142,
      "versionNonce": 428496097,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1766797964871,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Importance of Security \n● Ensuring Robust Authentication and Authorization: Implementing \nstrong security measures helps safeguard applications from\nunauthorized \naccess. \n● Comprehensive Security Measures: Applications should be\nprotected at \nmultiple levels to prevent vulnerabilities. \n● Security as a Growing Concern: Modern applications face\nincreasing risks \nfrom various attack vectors, making it essential to stay\nproactive.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Importance of Security \n● Ensuring Robust Authentication and Authorization: Implementing \nstrong security measures helps safeguard applications from unauthorized \naccess. \n● Comprehensive Security Measures: Applications should be protected at \nmultiple levels to prevent vulnerabilities. \n● Security as a Growing Concern: Modern applications face increasing risks \nfrom various attack vectors, making it essential to stay proactive.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "S6XACZklCz_V8NhDnQsbT",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 487.2857666015625,
      "y": 725.857177734375,
      "width": 924,
      "height": 200,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bef",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1585902209,
      "version": 177,
      "versionNonce": 641198017,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1766798100461,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Now our webapp / backend api are expose to threats on internet \nand in order to identify those threat oswap(https://owasp.org/)\nOWASP, or the Open Worldwide Application Security Project, \nis a global non-profit foundation focused on improving software security by \nproviding free, open-source resources, tools, documentation, and community support \nfor developers, security professionals, and organizations to build and maintain \nsecure applications. Its most famous output is the OWASP Top 10, a list identifying \nthe most critical web application security risks and how to mitigate them.  ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Now our webapp / backend api are expose to threats on internet \nand in order to identify those threat oswap(https://owasp.org/)\nOWASP, or the Open Worldwide Application Security Project, \nis a global non-profit foundation focused on improving software security by \nproviding free, open-source resources, tools, documentation, and community support \nfor developers, security professionals, and organizations to build and maintain \nsecure applications. Its most famous output is the OWASP Top 10, a list identifying \nthe most critical web application security risks and how to mitigate them.  ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "fvEdlaEop4pFrK9JDf4c6",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 496.0001220703125,
      "y": 1008.7857666015625,
      "width": 704,
      "height": 75,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "beg",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 748914959,
      "version": 84,
      "versionNonce": 749222145,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1766798151153,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The OWASP Top 10 is a standard awareness document for developers\nand web application security. It represents a broad consensus\nabout the most critical security risks to web applications.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The OWASP Top 10 is a standard awareness document for developers and web application security. It represents a broad consensus about the most critical security risks to web applications.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "riQLi6AEyuFau2RWpoZCz",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 477.57147216796875,
      "y": 1108.2857971191406,
      "width": 856.285888671875,
      "height": 500,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "beh",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 987904975,
      "version": 133,
      "versionNonce": 572320673,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1766798188922,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The Open Web Application Security Project (OWASP) highlights the most \ncritical security risks for web applications. The 2021 Top 10 list includes: \n1. Broken Access Control \n2. Cryptographic Failures (e.g., use of deprecated algorithms like MD5, \nSHA1) \n3. Injection Attacks: \n○ Example: Using unvalidated input in SQL queries, such as: \nSELECT * FROM users WHERE username = 'userInput'; \n○ Risk: Queries that allow username = 'navin' OR 1=1 can expose all \nuser data. \n○ Prevention: Use prepared statements to prevent SQL injection. \n\n\n4. Insecure Design \n5. Security Misconfiguration (e.g., default configurations in use) \n6. Vulnerable and Outdated Components \n7. Identification and Authentication Failures \n8. Software and Data Integrity Failures \n9. Security Logging and Monitoring Failures \n10. Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF) ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The Open Web Application Security Project (OWASP) highlights the most \ncritical security risks for web applications. The 2021 Top 10 list includes: \n1. Broken Access Control \n2. Cryptographic Failures (e.g., use of deprecated algorithms like MD5, \nSHA1) \n3. Injection Attacks: \n○ Example: Using unvalidated input in SQL queries, such as: \nSELECT * FROM users WHERE username = 'userInput'; \n○ Risk: Queries that allow username = 'navin' OR 1=1 can expose all \nuser data. \n○ Prevention: Use prepared statements to prevent SQL injection. \n\n\n4. Insecure Design \n5. Security Misconfiguration (e.g., default configurations in use) \n6. Vulnerable and Outdated Components \n7. Identification and Authentication Failures \n8. Software and Data Integrity Failures \n9. Security Logging and Monitoring Failures \n10. Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF) ",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
