    },
    {
      "id": "zZmDPvIs1xXllcphLnFB_",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 500.0678597822174,
      "y": 8847.032843415103,
      "width": 1081.7429749113344,
      "height": 325,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bfF",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1697936111,
      "version": 99,
      "versionNonce": 1012218415,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1766911058174,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "2.Authorization\n\nAuthorization is the process of determining what you can and cannot do within the app after you've\nlogged in. Even though you're authenticated and allowed into the app, your permissions decide\nwhether you can access certain features or areas, like editing your settings or accessing the\nadmin panel. Authorization ensures that users can only interact with the parts of the application\nthey have the rights to, safeguarding sensitive information and features.\n\nImagine:\n\nYou've successfully logged into your favorite social media app. Now, you want to do different\nthings within the app, like viewing your profile, editing settings, or accessing admin features.\nHere’s how authorization comes into play:",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "2.Authorization\n\nAuthorization is the process of determining what you can and cannot do within the app after you've logged in. Even though you're authenticated and allowed into the app, your permissions decide whether you can access certain features or areas, like editing your settings or accessing the admin panel. Authorization ensures that users can only interact with the parts of the application they have the rights to, safeguarding sensitive information and features.\n\nImagine:\n\nYou've successfully logged into your favorite social media app. Now, you want to do different things within the app, like viewing your profile, editing settings, or accessing admin features. Here’s how authorization comes into play:",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
